WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.904
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.037 --> 00:06.115
See how curators grade evidence.

00:06.633 --> 00:09.740
How strong is the evidence for an entity?

00:09.873 --> 00:15.182
An entity is one gene,
one mode of inheritance and one disease.

00:15.315 --> 00:20.573
To set its evidence category,
curators count cases, combine criteria,

00:20.706 --> 00:22.851
and weigh the doubts.

00:23.367 --> 00:26.684
A Definitive entity needs a publication.

00:26.817 --> 00:30.186
Then count each individual and family once.

00:30.320 --> 00:33.425
Ten or more cases with <i>de novo</i> variants,

00:33.558 --> 00:36.577
five or more autosomal recessive families,

00:36.711 --> 00:40.400
or three or more families with X-chromosomal variants:

00:40.533 --> 00:42.812
each is a clear-cut frequency,

00:42.945 --> 00:46.761
and no further criteria are needed.

00:47.267 --> 00:53.790
For <i>ANKRD11</i> and KBG syndrome,
the synopsis reports <i>de novo</i>

00:53.923 --> 00:57.903
and some inherited variants
in more than 300 individuals.

00:58.036 --> 01:01.322
That is far more than ten <i>de novo</i> cases.

01:01.455 --> 01:04.396
This entity is Definitive.

01:04.900 --> 01:08.043
If the count falls short, combine.

01:08.176 --> 01:13.468
A strong frequency criterion,
such as three patients with <i>de novo</i> variants,

01:13.601 --> 01:19.564
needs a partner: one strong genetic criterion,
one strong clinical criterion,

01:19.697 --> 01:23.121
or at least two moderate criteria.

01:23.633 --> 01:27.508
The category belongs to the entity, not to the gene.

01:27.641 --> 01:33.742
<i>SETD1B</i> has two entities:
the autosomal dominant one is Definitive,

01:33.875 --> 01:37.325
the autosomal recessive one is Moderate.

01:37.833 --> 01:40.206
Open the recessive entity.

01:40.340 --> 01:43.656
Its synopsis reports bi-allelic missense variants

01:43.789 --> 01:49.370
in 3 independent individuals:
a strong frequency criterion.

01:49.503 --> 01:53.255
Without a partner, it is Moderate: better than Limited,

01:53.389 --> 01:56.444
but not enough for Definitive.

01:56.967 --> 02:01.931
<i>ZCCHC8</i> has one recessive
family with a nonsense variant.

02:02.064 --> 02:08.829
No functional evidence is recorded,
so this entity is Limited.

02:09.333 --> 02:13.693
In borderline cases,
weigh the possible negative criteria.

02:13.826 --> 02:17.280
First, an old publication, never confirmed.

02:17.413 --> 02:20.487
Second, doubtful publication quality.

02:20.621 --> 02:24.304
Third, new evidence against the gene or its variants,

02:24.437 --> 02:30.090
such as constraint scores
from the Genome Aggregation Database, gnomAD.

02:30.224 --> 02:35.134
If the association is contradicted, consider Refuted.

02:35.667 --> 02:40.783
For <i>PGA5</i>, one individual was described in 2010,

02:40.916 --> 02:43.584
with no further publications since.

02:43.718 --> 02:49.653
In gnomAD, the gene is tolerant
to missense and loss-of-function variants.

02:49.786 --> 02:52.639
This entity is Refuted.

02:53.167 --> 02:56.765
The gene page shows the gnomAD scores.

02:56.898 --> 03:03.898
Loss-of-function variants are not depleted:
15.9 expected, 18 observed.

03:05.033 --> 03:09.939
Remember to count each
individual and family once, per entity.

03:10.072 --> 03:13.773
A clear-cut frequency needs no further criteria.

03:13.907 --> 03:17.985
Otherwise, a strong frequency criterion needs a partner.

03:18.118 --> 03:22.006
In borderline cases, weigh the doubts.

03:22.533 --> 03:28.488
Find all the rules in the documentation
chapter Curation criteria.
